   one colored foldout plate, and a stated height of 28 cm. [1][3]             
 • The so-called Nestor Ring was reportedly found in 1924, but its authenticity
   remains a matter of scholarly dispute. [4]                                  
 • Historical scholarly opinion on the Nestor Ring has been divided: Sir Arthur
   Evans accepted it as authentic, while many other scholars regarded it as a  
   forgery; some later scholars reportedly renewed claims for its authenticity.
   [4]                                                                         
